Package: secure-delete
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: securely delete files or whole storage devices
 Overwrites files or block devices before deleting them, using standard
 sanitization methods: zeros, random data, DoD 5220.22-M, Gutmann,
 NIST 800-88, BSI, VSITR and others. It can verify the last pass, handles
 sparse files and refuses to wipe mounted devices.
 .
 This package contains the command-line tool.

Package: secure-delete-gui
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         secure-delete (= ${binary:Version}),
         hicolor-icon-theme,
         libdtk6declarative,
         pkexec,
         qml6-module-qtquick,
         qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
         qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs,
         qml6-module-qtquick-layouts
Description: securely delete files or storage devices - Deepin interface
 Graphical front-end for secure-delete built with Qt 6 and DTK6 (Deepin
 Tool Kit). Choose a file or a detected storage device, pick a wipe method
 and follow the progress. Wiping a device asks for an administrator
 password through polkit (pkexec).
